  internal_note = {Cited once, in the Discussion, to place this atlas relative to a contemporaneous credibility assessment in the same clinical domain. PREPRINT, not peer-reviewed as of 2026-08-10: no journal_ref and no arXiv DOI in the arXiv API response, and no Crossref hit on the title. Cited as a preprint deliberately, as cornish2023 also was until its 2026 publication in the Journal of Machine Learning Research. Its own acknowledgement records review by Pras Pathmanathan (U.S. FDA); one co-author is employed by Draegerwerk and declares it. VERIFICATION DEPTH: FULL TEXT READ 2026-08-10, all 22 pages of main text plus the reference list (arXiv:2607.06210v1, 7 July 2026). What it supports, verbatim: "a sensitivity analysis and uncertainty quantification of the baseline patient model must be performed before validation can begin"; and the figure captions scope the analysis themselves, "sensitivity analysis of the lung mechanics and gas exchange submodels" and "of the respiratory center submodels". WHAT MUST NOT BE WRITTEN, and why: the full list of sampled parameters is in "Table 1 and 4 of the supplement material", a separate document NOT read. Every parameter named in the reported results is internal (lung and chest-wall elastance, airway resistance, dead space, shunt fraction, cardiac output, chemoreceptor gains, respiratory-failure severity, chemical set point) and no sensitivity or uncertainty passage mentions a ventilator setting -- but that is evidence of what they REPORT, not proof of what they did not sample. So the manuscript states what the paper reports and never asserts that ventilator settings were absent from their analysis. Method differs from ours (Latin hypercube sampling, Monte Carlo, Spearman rank correlation, versus Morris elementary effects with sigma/mu*); state this as a difference of method and objective, never as a ranking.}
